-- Test: sibling sections defining the same name must STILL be ambiguous.
--
-- Lexical scoping only prefers bindings on the current section's ancestry
-- (same section, parent, ..., top level). Sibling subsections §§ b and §§ c
-- are NOT on each other's ancestry, and from their common ancestor § a neither
-- is nearer than the other, so an unqualified reference remains ambiguous.
-- To disambiguate, the reference must be qualified (a.b.x or a.c.x).

§ a
-- Referenced directly in § a, the common ancestor of siblings §§ b and §§ c.
-- (Forward references are allowed by the type checker.)
#CHECK x

§§ b
ASSUME x IS A BOOLEAN

§§ c
ASSUME x IS A NUMBER
